From 9c53bf5d163b2e8e812481c7e99e462c7966c1bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:57:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 215/403] Part: Part.exportPptx / Part.exportSvg, colours from
 dicts and from the FCStd file

  Part.exportPptx(objects, "out.pptx", view="iso", edges="outline", group=True,
                  lineWidth=0.5, deflection=0, colors=None)
      -> {"faces", "edges", "shapes", "groups"}
  Part.exportSvg(objects, "out.svg", view="iso", edges="all", group=True,
                 lineWidth=1.0, width=1000, deflection=0, colors=None)

objects as for Part.renderImage: shapes, meshes, document objects, a whole
document, and dicts {"shape"|"mesh"|"object": ..., "color": (r, g, b),
"faceColors": [...], "group": "a/b/c", "label": name}, so headless scripts
can set colours and groups.

Colours (renderImage, projectVisible, SVG, JSON and PPTX alike): a dict's
"color"/"faceColors" first, then colors={Name|Label|index: rgb}, then the
object's view colours, then the palette (colors="palette" forces it).
Headless there is no ViewObject, so PartViews.object_colors reads them from
the GuiDocument.xml in the FCStd file: ShapeAppearance (one material, or
one per face), ShapeColor/DiffuseColor of files before 1.0, and links
(OverrideMaterial, else the linked object's colours).  Per-face colours are
new in the C++ scene (SceneItem::faceColors, dict key "faceColors"), and
renderImage given document objects asks PartViews for their colours.

Tests: a file saved headless and given the GuiDocument.xml the GUI writes
(1.x materials, 0.21 ShapeColor + DiffuseColor, links with and without
override); the same values come out in the GUI (checked under xvfb with
a file saved by the GUI).  Dict colours and per-face colours in PPTX fills
and in renderImage pixels.

